;; re-derived from this worktree's own op numbering. add-debug-bound-internal
;; alone stays held in that class -- see below, it needs more than config.
;; The remaining 8 of jak3's 46 defun-debugs still absent from this file do
;; not decode clean and stay held, grouped by the failure class the
;; decompiler reported (op numbers are this rung's own scoped-decode run,
;; reproducible via the recipe in docs/jakx-bringup-quickstart.md's
;; "Scratch-only scoped decodes" section):
;;
;; - Full expression-builder failure ("function was not converted to
;;   expressions. Cannot decompile.", no body at all): add-debug-arc,
;;   add-debug-points.
;; - Raw MIPS/VU fallback (decompiler gives up on expression-building partway
;;   through and dumps local-vars plus rlet register soup, most of the body
;;   typed <uninitialized>): add-debug-cross, debug-pad-display (also "failed
;;   type prop at 46" and "Failed to guess label use for L288"),
;;   add-debug-cursor (also "Failed to guess stack use for 16").
;; - Single bad memory access, but not a simple register/stack re-type:
;;   add-debug-bound-internal (multiple: failed type prop at 119, "Failed to
;;   guess label use for L270", four "Unsupported inline assembly instruction
;;   kind" srl hits). jak3's own twin needs no type_casts/stack_structures
;;   entry at all because it sidesteps the wall entirely -- it uses raw
;;   vf27-class rlet register access plus a dedicated mips2c port
;;   (set-sky-vf27, itself needed because add-debug-bound-internal "sneaks
;;   an extra value in vf27") and further mips2c ports for its
;;   draw-boundary-polygon/render-boundary-quad/render-boundary-tri
;;   callees. That is a mips2c-port undertaking (issue #133's gates), not a
;;   config pass, so it is out of scope for this rung's bounded config work
;;   and stays held with a from-scratch op cite above rather than a stale
;;   one.
;; - Stack-slot size mismatch (declared size 4, actual access size 16, three
;;   separate sites all at offset 32): add-debug-yrot-vector.
;; - Clean body, but its only callee is itself unlanded: bugfix? decodes
;;   clean and calls only qword-read-time, which does not (COP0 performance
;;   counter reads via "mfc0 v1, Count" / "mfc0 a1, Count", flagged
;;   "Unsupported inline assembly instruction kind", the same class as the
;;   already-extern-only cpu-delay). Landing bugfix? without a real
;;   qword-read-time body would be the e2 class (a definition whose only
;;   callee still links to 0), so it stays held with its callee.
;;
;; Retirement condition per class: the first two classes need a hand port
;; citing a twin (add-debug-arc has one in jak3; add-debug-points and
;; qword-read-time/cpu-delay's COP0 reads do not) or a mips2c port for the
;; COP0-register pair; add-debug-bound-internal needs the mips2c-port chain
;; described above; add-debug-yrot-vector's stack-slot mismatch and
;; bugfix?/qword-read-time are unchanged from the heldarms rung's own
;; assessment.
